  "summary": "A traditional Moroccan house centered around an interior courtyard garden.",
  "description": "Characterized by inward-facing design with a central courtyard surrounded by rooms, providing privacy and coolness in hot climates. Developed over centuries to adapt to the Mediterranean climate while incorporating Islamic principles of domestic space.",
  "culturalContext": "The riad — Moroccan courtyard house with an inner garden — matured in Marrakesh and Fez's medinas as Islamic family law and climate demanded inward privacy: blind walls outside, orange trees and fountains inside under high ceilings, with zellij tile, carved cedar and tadelakt plaster. Restoration booms from the 1990s turned hundreds into guest houses, exporting the riad as a global hospitality template.",
